WEBVTT

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.810
Youth novels... and a how-to book?

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.680
Hey! Who said you could look at my books?

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.440
Pitiful child...

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.650
I can't let you read these, Shiki!

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.570
If you want to debut as a new you in 
high school, start with your looks!

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.210
Here, untuck your shirt!

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:20.330
Whoa! H-Hey!

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:21.550
Come on!

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.200
I-I'm going!

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.540
Take care.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.230
If you want to get contacts, 
see an eye doctor first!

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.540
<i>I'm not getting contacts!</i>

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.900
<i>That's not what I care about, Mom.</i>

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.130
<i>I, Koshiyama Shiki, age 15,</i>

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.510
<i>have learned of a new world.</i>

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.330
<b>Fastest
Finger
First</b>

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.730
<b>Question 4: "A Mysterious Beauty Appears,"</b>

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.730
<i>It started with the meet at the 
welcome ceremony for new students,</i>

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.360
<i>and then there was the Four Schools 
Quiz Meet at Sekigawata High School.</i>

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.740
<i>I'm sure I'll find yet another 
new world at my next meet.</i>

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.200
<i>I can't help feeling that way!</i>

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:24.740
I want to do quiz bowl 
with you, Koshiyama-kun.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:25.710
I'm telling you...

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.750
to do quiz bowl!

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.960
<i>After being asked so enthusiastically,</i>

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.920
<i>what choice do I have?</i>

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.690
Watch it!

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.200
<i>H-How could I get so giddy?</i>

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:46.560
<i>Is that...</i>

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:47.810
<i>Fukami-san?</i>

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.270
<b>Pedestrians
and Bicycles
Only</b>

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:50.630
<i>The friend manual, step 1:</i>

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.070
<i>Start with a greeting.</i>

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.660
G-Good morning!

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.730
Oh, Koshiyama-kun.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.180
Wait!

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.700
Can I ride on the back?

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.450
Huh?

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.660
<i>Isn't this a bit too big of a step forward?</i>

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.700
Koshiyama-kun, go faster! We'll be late!

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.620
Eh... buh... heavy...

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.000
Heavy?

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.140
<i>Wh-What?</i>

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.630
You're so light, Koshiyama-kun!

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.650
<i>Isn't this... wrong?</i>

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:27.570
Morning!

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.210
Mor... Huh?

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.770
<i>We totally stand out!</i>

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.270
Oh, it's Sasajima-senpai.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.570
Good morning!

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.480
M-Morning...

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.050
Hey, morning.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.250
Did you see that?

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.410
Yeah.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.850
Th-The quiz circle's president 
is riding with a cute girl?!

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.020
And you guys, too?!

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.720
Koshiyama-kun!

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.490
Morning!

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:06.930
Uh... M-Morning...

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.750
Is that what the Quiz Bowl Circle's about?

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.010
Does joining it make you 
a hit with the girls?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.500
And what about that quiz 
meet thing? How'd it go?

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.650
That was a pretty bold invitation 
they gave you last week.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.320
<i>Are they interested in quiz bowl?</i>

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.190
The best clubs are the co-ed ones, for sure.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.890
Just join the quiz circle!

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.570
No way. I'm not that smart.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.940
You join it.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.540
I'm not joining a club that 
makes me use my head!

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.540
<i>Yeah, I guess not.</i>

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.930
You're right. Quiz bowl isn't 
something any idiot can do.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.000
Huh?

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:37.930
F-Fukami-san?

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:40.630
You've gotta be a <i>big</i> idiot!

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.090
<b>Big Idiot</b>

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.050
Library

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.890
I just get so weird when 
it comes to quiz bowl.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.310
People already think I'm some weird 
girl who's into quiz bowl...

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.060
<i>She did realize it, then?</i>

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.440
Does being around me make 
you feel embarrassed, too?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.180
Why else would you eat lunch in here?

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.900
<i>Actually, I've always eaten in here...</i>

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:09.930
<i>In truth, I should've said 
something back to them.</i>

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.570
Sorry for interrupting your lunch.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.500
<i>I can't think of anything 
to say to her, even now.</i>

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:22.760
Actually, after school...

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.630
I thought I'd check out 
the quiz circle, too.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.010
Okay. I'll be waiting.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.610
<i>She smiled...</i>

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.560
<i>A-All right!</i>

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.650
<b>Small Classroom B</b>

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.650
Class 1-D!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.420
Koshiyama Shiki!

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:43.890
Inoue Daisuke!

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.770
Thanks for having us!

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:47.970
So you're here.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:49.030
Thanks for coming!

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.870
So you're gonna join, too?

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.050
I could ask you the same.

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:55.010
I'm glad you asked!

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:55.830
Uh, I didn't...

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.230
"I want to do quiz bowl 
with you, Inoue-kun."

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:02.920
What man could turn down 
a request like that?!

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.440
So now we have four members?

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.880
One more until we're promoted to a club!

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.680
Well, now that our new 
members are with us...

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.890
I believe the quiz meet at 
Sekigawata gave you a taste,

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.180
but do you have any questions?

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.140
<i>Questions...</i>

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.690
<i>What's your relationship to 
that girl from this morning?</i>

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:22.760
I do.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.270
<i>You're gonna ask?!</i>

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.030
Fukami-kun.

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:29.780
How can we win in quiz bowl?

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.540
That's just like Fukami-san.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.540
"Win," eh?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:37.790
You can't.

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.210
There's no need for quiz bowl 
that you play only to win.

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:44.200
What does that mean?

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:49.200
Isn't winning by getting the right answers 
what competitive quiz bowl is about?

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.270
Yes, the nature of competition is 
to determine a winner and a loser.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:55.430
Fukami-kun, do you like quiz bowl?

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:56.840
Of course.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:00.270
Then why concern yourself 
with winning or losing?

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:03.890
<i>This is kind of unexpected.</i>

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:06.150
<i>As passionate as Sasajima-senpai 
is about quiz bowl,</i>

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.390
<i>I thought he'd be determined to win.</i>

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.580
I love it. That's why I don't want to lose.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.800
I see. Then let me rephrase that.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.750
You three don't yet need quiz 
bowl that's only about winning!

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.720
Before you worry about winning and losing,

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.630
you first need to learn the 
true nature of quiz bowl!

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.660
What sort of quiz bowl do you want to play?

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:30.860
What will you strive for?

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.840
How should you learn with all that in mind?

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.550
It's all up to you!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:38.680
Of course, that goes for me, too.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.640
<i>Me?</i>

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.030
<i>The kind of quiz bowl I want to play...</i>

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.190
I...

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.070
Before I worry about defeating others, 
I want to defeat quiz bowl itself.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:53.500
Quiz bowl itself?

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.990
I'm a complete beginner who 
knows nothing about quiz bowl.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.870
Being unable to answer 
when I know the question

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.130
and answering wrong make me frustrated.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.840
I want to remember questions I answered 
wrong so I can get them right next time.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:08.840
It's just like you said, Fukami-san.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:12.220
After I got a correct answer like that,

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.210
I want to learn more about quiz bowl,

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.050
and I want to answer more questions.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.530
I want to give correct answers.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:23.030
That's... what I think.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.050
Koshiyama-kun...

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.310
Well, it's true that we don't know 
any classic questions or anything.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.750
I couldn't do a thing when they asked those.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:33.250
Y-Yeah, exactly!

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.370
Classics...

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:36.540
Senpai, do we still have these?

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.160
Of course.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.620
This is a set of 300 class 
questions that I chose.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.330
The most common questions, right?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.870
I think they're just the 
right level for beginners.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.840
<b>Quiz Bowl
Circle</b>

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.840
<b>300 Classic Questions</b>

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.840
Let me be clear that simply memorizing 
all these is not the answer.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.460
You need to understand the 
structure of the questions

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.880
and become accustomed to 
how they're introduced.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:55.910
Structure?

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.050
Introduced?

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:58.350
You want to know?

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.010
Yes!

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:03.870
There are several ways to 
categorize quiz bowl questions.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:07.230
One of them is "straight or parallel."

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.230
Straight or parallel?

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:13.510
The most standard format is 
the "straight question."

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:15.690
They begin with a subtle hint,

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:18.240
and the range of possible answers 
becomes increasingly smaller.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.490
Maybe that's too complicated for beginners.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.970
Then you will learn the basics of quiz bowl

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:26.790
through a fastest finger challenge!

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.170
Yeah!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.000
<b>Whipping Up 300 Questions</b>

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.010
<b>Ba-dum
Ba-dum</b>

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.340
So... what is this?

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:36.730
A calculator.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.050
We can see that.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.680
Each of you, put a finger on 
it and press at the same time.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.200
943?

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.900
Oh, I get it.

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:47.390
This will tell us who "buzzed in" first.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.570
Wait, don't we have buzzers?

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:50.110
No.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.650
But what about the ones 
at the welcome ceremony?

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.820
I rented those.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:59.090
I was really on edge when you pounded 
on your button that one time.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:02.190
Aside from being rentals, 
those things are expensive!

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:04.100
How much would it cost to buy a set?

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.670
There are a few different 
ways to acquire them,

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:09.040
but if you purchase them 
through proper channels...

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:14.760
Control Box

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:14.760
4 Buzzers

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:14.100
A complete set would be 50,000... 
No, some run as high as 100,000 yen.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:14.760
A hundred—

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:17.410
Couldn't we get a used set somewhere?

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:18.720
I'm looking for one now.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.430
Let's begin.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:21.510
Okay.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:24.930
Question.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.940
The three great festivals of Kyoto are

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:31.870
May's Hollyhock Festival, July's Gion Festival, 
and October's Festival of what?

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.270
Nine's first. That's me!

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:35.400
Festival of Ages.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.240
Correct.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:36.990
Yes!

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:40.450
<b>Basic Question Structures 
Straight or Parallel 

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:40.450
This type of question is 
known as "numerated format."

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:50.460
<b>Q: The three elements
of music are
melody, rhythm,
and what?
[Harmony]</b>

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:50.460
<b>Q: The three great festivals
of Kyoto are
May's Hollyhock Festival,
July's Gion Festival,
and October's Festival of what? 
[Festival of Ages]</b>

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:45.130
The three elements of music and the three 
obligations of all citizens fit this category.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:49.020
The first syllable of the second item in 
the list is the determining point, right?

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:49.920
Oh...

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.640
Next question.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.480
French for "flash of lightning,"

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:57.670
a long, thin pastry topped with 
chocolate is known by what name?

00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.160
Yes! It's me!

00:10:59.160 --> 00:10:59.880
Éclair!

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:05.850
<b>Basic Question Structures 
Straight or Parallel 

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:00.920
Correct.

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:04.480
This is a "foreign language question" 
in which you must give the word

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.850
based on its original meaning.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.680
<b>Q: Italian for "in the
manner of the chapel,"
music with no
instrumental accompaniment is known by what name? 
[A Capella]</b>

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.680
<b>Q: French for
"flash of lightning,"
a long, thin pastry
topped with chocolate
is known by what name? 
[Éclair]</b>

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.130
These are Fukami-kun's specialty.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:08.680
Yeah!

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:09.810
Question.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.840
"As Gregor Samsa awoke one 
morning out of restless dreams"

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.690
is the opening line of which 
novel by Franz Kafka?

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.320
Yes! It's me!

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.890
Damn it, Koshiyama! 
You pulled the calculator to you!

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:24.110
No, I didn't!

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:25.450
Don't call it a calculator!

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:26.790
Koshiyama.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.200
The answer is <i>The Metamorphosis</i>.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:35.460
<b>Basic Question Structures 
Straight or Parallel 

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:29.340
Correct.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:33.370
Novels with memorable first lines 
unlike those of other works

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:35.460
are often the subject of 
"first line questions."

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:41.470
<b>Q: "Because of a hereditary
recklessness, I have been
playing always a losing game
since my childhood"
is the first line of
which Natsume Soseki novel? 
[Botchan]</b>

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:36.990
Like <i>Das Gemeine</i>, too?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:41.470
<b>Q: "I fell in love.
This was something new."
is the first line of which
literary work
by Dazai Osamu? 
[Das Gemeine]</b>

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:37.730
Yes.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.750
I don't know any of this stuff.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:41.470
Aren't there any that work for me?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:45.180
And in addition to these types of 
straight questions, there's this.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.220
<b>Parallel</b>

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.220
Parallel...

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:58.940
<b>The 19th century musician
known as the
"magician of the piano"
was Liszt, while the
one known as the
"poet of the piano"
was whom? 
[Chopin]</b>

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:58.940
<b>The nation with the
largest land area is Russia,
and the nation with
the smallest land area is which? 
[Vatican City]</b>

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.740
Questions in which the first and second half

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:52.610
are connected by words 
such as "and" or "while,"

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.800
where the question asked is something 
different from that given the first half

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.130
are called "parallel questions."

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.940
I've struggled with those a lot...

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:00.150
Question.

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:05.520
In anime "CV," the abbreviation used for voice actors, "C" stands for "character,"

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.620
and "V" stands for what?

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:08.580
Yes!

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.750
This is the one I got before!

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:11.390
Voice!

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:12.030
Correct.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:13.040
Score!

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:17.050
Parallel questions can have 
complicated structures, so be alert.

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:20.250
Memorizing structures using 
classic questions, huh?

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.450
So even if we encounter a 
question that isn't so common,

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.050
we can make use of this.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.470
Of course, memorizing the classics 
themselves is highly worthwhile, too.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:33.020
<b>Q: When asked, "Why climb the mountain?",
which English mountaineer answered,
"Because it's there"?       A: George Mallory</b>

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:33.020
Some of them, like "why climb," 
have become fixed questions themselves.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.760
Fixed questions?

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:36.190
Even among the classics,

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:39.390
questions whose wording 
remains constant every time

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:42.170
flow naturally, giving neither too 
much nor too little information.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:44.780
You could say they are among the most 
complete questions in quiz bowl.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.350
I get it. Complete, huh?

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:52.660
Yeah, it does seem like a lot of classic 
questions draw interest to themselves.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.670
I know what you mean! 
They seem hard at first,

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:59.130
but you've actually learned them in 
school or as some bit of trivia!

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:00.460
Exactly.

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:04.340
Questions that can draw the 
interest of those answering

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:07.770
survive through the ages without 
ever being weeded out.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.940
Since they're asked all the 
time, everyone knows them.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:13.790
And since everyone knows them, 
they're asked all the time.

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.940
That repetition makes them classics.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:20.820
You could say that classic questions 
carry the very history of quiz bowl!

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:23.170
Classic questions are awesome!

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:27.320
I feel like I've had a glimpse of history 
along with quiz players' love for quiz bowl!

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:31.710
Senpai, give us the next question!

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.880
Make it one about idols, my best subject!

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:35.390
Some history and literature, too!

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:37.070
Please!

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:41.590
<b>Haruki Academy High School</b>

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.590
Buzou High School? Where's that?

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:44.010
It's a regular prefectural 
high school in Saitama.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.090
Apparently they have a quiz bowl team now,

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:49.410
and the guy who started it is...

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:50.750
What? Who?

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.260
Applying for English Level 
2 Certification Classes

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:53.070
Get this. It's Sasajima Gakuto!

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:58.960
Seriously? What's he doing at 
a prefectural school, anyway?

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.380
No idea...

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.930
What? You curious?

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:07.130
Hey, don't ignore us, Fukami!

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:10.660
All right, everyone.

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.660
Today is our club's review meeting.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.410
<b>Press button for service</b>

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:14.620
Have you decided what to order?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.410
Yes.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:17.490
Then go ahead.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:19.670
Yes!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.620
Lost again...

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:24.920
I think the button was a little 
closer to Kouzuki-san that time.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:30.950
I only wish you could buzz in so decisively 
in actual meets, Kouzuki-san.

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.440
You as well, Kenmochi-san and Kogawa-san.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.310
Move more lightly, using your full bodies.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.070
Buzzing in is a sport.

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:37.820
Right.

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:40.270
Why the listless responses?

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.160
As one of the few quiz bowl teams 
from an all girls' school,

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:45.000
and as students of Asagaoka,

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.900
we should act in a way that 
doesn't bring shame upon us.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:47.900
<i>Here she goes again.</i>

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:52.170
Last week's meet at Sekigawata 
should have been very inspiring.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:56.000
I guess the one to keep an eye 
on is Mikuriya-kun from Miyaura.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:06.380
<b>Mikuriya</b>

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.420
That's right.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:00.150
He possesses a great deal of talent,

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:02.710
and he can't stand losing.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:06.380
<b>Sasaki</b>

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.630
But one mustn't overlook Sasaki-kun,

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.380
the middle school first-year from Sekigawata.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:09.700
I thought Sekigawata's club 
president was amazing.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:10.630
Huh?

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:14.370
Watching him look out for his junior 
was like watching two close brothers.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:17.390
Niina

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:17.390
Sasaki

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:15.840
It was such a soothing sight.

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.390
Did that happen?

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.330
How naïve of you.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.900
I suppose you beginners don't know it yet,

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:26.360
Ashiya

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:26.360
Niina

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:26.360
but Niina of Sekigawata has a 
partner at Miyaura named Ashiya.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.620
they've been buddies since 
they were first-years.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:30.930
Nii x Ashi, then?

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.510
Really? Them?

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:36.370
I think Inoue-kun from Buzou 
is a well-kept secret, though!

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.440
There it is! You have such 
strong taste, Kogawa-senpai!

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:40.490
Really?

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:42.010
Better run, Inoue-kun!

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:43.720
You're both naïve.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:44.320
<i>I want to go home...</i>

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:46.990
What makes one great is the ability to make 
a tasty dish out of any ingredients.

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:48.350
Well said!

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.010
<b>Maririn</b>

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.010
There's something I want 
to talk to you about...

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:49.340
Let's all work hard.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.010
Yeah!

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:52.720
Maririn!

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:55.160
Yukicchi!

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:59.040
You really had me worried 
at that last quiz meet.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:01.000
You kept glaring at me in the beginning.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.600
I thought you saw me as an enemy.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:05.060
Not at all. Just as a rival.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.870
You're smarter than me, after all,

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.070
and you went off to Asagaoka without me.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:14.300
You failed because you focused too much 
on quiz bowl and not enough on studying.

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:16.820
I feel better now, though.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:19.240
You seem to be having a good time at Buzou.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:23.960
Yeah. Koshiyama-kun and Inoue-kun 
both joined our quiz bowl circle.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:28.930
With a quiz nut like you next to 
them, anyone would be inspired.

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.610
A "nut"? Come on...

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:34.800
I had a great time in middle 
school because of that.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:35.930
Yukicchi...

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.600
Hey, didn't you say you 
wanted to ask me something?

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:40.640
Oh, yeah.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:44.430
Yukicchi, you don't have any 
extra buzzer sets, do you?

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.270
A calculator?!

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.280
A calculator!

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:52.150
You use real buzzers at Asagaoka, right?

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:55.280
Yeah, but we don't have enough to lend out.

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.390
They cost 100,000 yen, huh?

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.550
Are they really that expensive?

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:01.440
Maybe I'll get a part-time job.

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:04.980
A job? Good idea! 
That could really broaden your horizons!

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:05.970
My horizons?

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:08.500
Well, Asagaoka is a mission 
school, you know?

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:14.220
So we get a lot of religious knowledge 
in our day-to-day school lives.

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:14.220
Q: A tool consisting of a string of beads with a cross on it, used by Catholics when praying, is known by what name? 
Q: In Catholicism, the one who gives a newly baptized follower their "Christian name" is known by what title? 
Q: In Christianity, the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit are known by what collective name? 
Q: Jesus Christ was crucified in Jerusalem, on a hill known by what name? 
Q: In the New Testament, the Virgin Mary was informed that she would give birth to the Christ by an angel named what?

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:18.600
Knowledge you pick up in your daily 
life tends to stick with you.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.220
Gaining knowledge by working, huh?

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:22.650
That could work!

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:23.280
Right?

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.280
<i>This place really calms my mind.</i>

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:38.180
<i>I might have underestimated classic 
questions a bit at first.</i>

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:40.990
<i>But the classics have their own appeal.</i>

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:45.370
<i>And even though I knew there'd be 
questions that I know the answers to,</i>

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:47.460
<i>I still got really into the 
race to hit the calculator—</i>

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.350
<i>I mean, the buzzer first.</i>

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:52.670
<i>When it's a genre I like, 
I want to answer even more.</i>

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.420
The regular meet in June is up next.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:57.760
Revenge!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.330
What's a regular meet?

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:03.020
I'll ask Sasajima-senpai next 
time the circle gets together.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:06.890
What? What's that?

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.360
Smells... good...

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:24.680
You're such a nice guy,

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.330
sharin' half of your lunch with me!

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:32.100
Luckily, I hadn't touched that part 
yet, so it should be clean...

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.170
No worries!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:37.180
<i>First a girl trips in front of me 
with her panties in plain sight,</i>

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.630
<i>and now a girl passes out 
starving in front of me...</i>

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:43.180
<i>Isn't a library supposed to 
be a more peaceful place?</i>

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:45.310
Really, thanks so much.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:48.350
I'll repay this debt to ya someday.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.840
That's okay. I always have 
about half left over anyway.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.650
Really? You're some light eater.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:55.320
You'll never grow big an' tall that way.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:59.610
<i>Come to think of it, she 
looks familiar somehow...</i>

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:04.740
Anyway, why're ya eatin' your 
lunch in a weird place like this?

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:07.120
B-Because I like books?

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.040
Huh... And what's that?

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.970
It's a collection of quiz bowl questions.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:12.790
Quiz bowl?

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:16.780
Oh! You're the <i>Das Gemeine</i> kid 
from the welcome ceremony!

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:20.330
<i>Someone I don't know knows who I am!</i>

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:24.870
Yep, it's good to have 
somethin' ya like to do.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:29.890
I got too wrapped up in my hobby and 
spent all my lunch money on it.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.900
Sequential
Control Circuits

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.900
Gettin' all the tools and 
stuff costs quite a bit.

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.920
Oh, so that's why you were starv—

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:35.960
Gotcha!

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.870
Koshiyama-kun?

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.790
F-Fukami-san!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:48.870
Whozzat?

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:52.460
There you are. Is this all—

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:54.340
Koshiyama?! You're—

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:56.150
U-Uh, look, this is...

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.010
Water!

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.260
Koshiyama-kun, you know that girl?

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.410
That's the girl who was with 
Sasajima-senpai, right?

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:08.270
Oh!

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:10.460
Your lunch...

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:12.980
That girl was eating your lunch?

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:16.230
Th-That was because she passed out 
from hunger in front of me...

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:17.610
So I gave her half...

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.690
I haven't even eaten your lunch yet!

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.990
Huh? What does that mean?

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:25.450
Wait, what did I mean by that?

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.420
Koshiyama!

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:30.540
Why do you get all the girls?!

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.290
Wait, it's not like that!

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:38.170
This is not fair!

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:43.920
Huh? You're kidding! 
Lunch is over already?

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:45.760
That girl isn't back yet...

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:47.720
Sequential Control
Circuits 
Practical Applications

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:47.720
And she left her book here...

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:49.420
Um...

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:53.090
<i>And Inoue won't stop crying...</i>

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.610
<i>I guess this is what youth is!</i>

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:32.950
Of the quiz question 
patterns we learned today,

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:37.210
<b>Parallel Questions</b>

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:36.700
parallel questions are a format 
with particular strategic value.

00:22:37.610 --> 00:22:39.460
Let's give it a try right now!

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:40.420
Right!

00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:41.510
Question.

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:45.300
A miniskirt, worn with knee-high socks,

00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:48.800
leaves a visible patch of thighs 
known as "absolute territory,"

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:48.800
Absolute Territory

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:52.010
while the area behind Sasajima-kun's 
glasses is called what?

00:22:52.010 --> 00:22:53.720
Huh?! Um, um...

00:22:54.080 --> 00:22:56.060
Buzz. Time's up.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:58.560
The answer is "invisible territory."

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:58.560
<b>Invisible Territory</b>

00:22:58.560 --> 00:22:59.780
Like we'd know that!
